**How it works**

- Uses Python's standard `html.parser.HTMLParser`, so no third-party packages are needed.
- `convert_charrefs=True` decodes entities like `&amp;` and `&#39;` in text data.
- When the first matching start tag is seen, the parser tracks nesting depth (so nested tags with the same name are handled correctly) and collects all text data until the matching end tag closes it.
- Text is returned exactly as found, without stripping whitespace. If you want surrounding whitespace removed, apply `.strip()` to the result, and you may also want to treat whitespace-only text as empty.

