    Compute the running (cumulative) sum down each numeric column of a table.

    `data` maps column names to equal-length lists of values. A column is
    numeric if every value in it is an int or float (bools are not counted
    as numeric). Non-numeric columns are ignored.

    Returns a dict mapping each numeric column name to its list of cumulative
    sums, preserving the original column order.

    Raises ValueError if the table has no rows or no numeric columns.
    """
