- A column counts as numeric only if every value is an `int` or `float` (booleans are excluded), and the column is non-empty.
- Each value's bin is `int((v - lo) * 10 / (hi - lo))`, with any index of 10 clamped to 9. This makes the maximum fall into the last bin, as required.
- If all values in a column are equal, the range has zero width. In that case I put every value in the first bin. The spec doesn't cover this case, so change it if you want a different convention.

