            d = math.hypot(xs[i] - xs[j], ys[i] - ys[j])
            if d > best:
                best = d
    return float(best)
```

This checks every pair of distinct positions, so it runs in O(n²) time. The example `max_pairwise_distance([2, 3, 4], [1, 5, 2])` returns `4.123105625617661`, the distance between (2, 1) and (3, 5). For inputs with many points, the convex hull followed by rotating calipers would give O(n log n), but the brute-force version is simpler and correct.

